    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0906" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins: Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Personal Representative</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Presidents
                        Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d439-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Casablanca</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-22">January 22, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi>—Giraud will have de Gaulle for
                        lunch.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d439-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0907" n="821" xml:id="pg821"/>
                <p>After lunch both men will be shut in a room for private confab.</p>
                <p>After that I think the PM should receive de Gaulle<anchor n="3" xml:id="d439-f3"
                    /> and then the PM should lead him over to the President.</p>
                <p>I think Giraud will be willing that the President be able to include in his
                    public statement something to effect that all Vichy racial laws will be
                    abolished in this area.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bob</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d439-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d439-f1-content">
                <p>The source text is handwritten.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d439-f2" n="2" xml:id="d439-f2-content">
                <p>This first de Gaulle–Giraud meeting appears to be the one described in de Gaulle,
                    p. 83, and Giraud, pp. 101–103.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d439-f3" n="3" xml:id="d439-f3-content">
                <p>Churchill did receive de Gaulle on January 22. For accounts of the meeting, see
                    de Gaulle, pp. 86–87, and Churchill, <hi rendition="#italic">Hinge of Fate</hi>,
                    pp. 681–682.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
